      "_note": "HEAVY 2026-07-16 (svccov-epas session, owner-approved SCP_RUN_HEAVY): dedicated 1-cluster campaign for the version-axis + new-instance-ops gap keys that epas-cluster-subops-a/b (database__subops-full.json) can't reach on a single already-newest-version cluster: epaspatchminorversion, epasshowinstance, epasmanualbackup, epasexportlog, epasremovebackuphistories (PF recheck), epasunsetbackup (PF recheck). Ported STRUCTURALLY from the live-proven mysql-cluster-version-upgrade / mariadb-cluster-version-upgrade (database__mysql.json / database__mariadb.json, 2026-07-16 svccov sessions) with epas's OWN live-verified specifics. LIVE GET /v1/engine-versions 2026-07-16 (svccov-epas session): contents[0]=17.7 id d058dc79a86842f9b558933e9d285b9f (newest major 17 minor), contents[1]=17.6 id e9f7306c6734479b865d0dd8b9b8c6d5, contents[2]=16.11 id dd6967f9a5ef4fcb9cb0db7546be57ee (newest major 16 minor), contents[3]=16.10, contents[4]=16.9, contents[5]=16.8 id 821110c054044f0188b0811e53ef9ed6 (oldest major 16 minor), contents[6..9]=15.15/15.14/15.13/15.12 -- ASSUMES this descending-by-recency order holds; re-derive indices from a fresh GET if a run shows a capture mismatch. epas has NO major-version-upgrade endpoint (confirmed absent from the catalog -- unlike mysql/mariadb which have PUT .../major-version-upgrade) so this lifecycle only proves the minor-patch axis: create the cluster on the OLDEST minor of major 16 (16.8, contents[5]) -> epaspatchminorversion jumps it to the NEWEST minor of the SAME major (16.11, contents[2]) -- deliberately NOT major 17, since a patch across majors is untested/risky and the known-blocked pattern is resending the cluster's OWN current version (400 'Unpatchable version' per the mysql/mariadb precedent), not a same-major minor jump. MinorPatchRequest body: {backup_before_upgrade: bool REQUIRED, software_version: string REQUIRED} per mysql/mariadb precedent (data/api_docs.json epaspatchminorversion model list both fields; doc's own request_example shows both too). epasshowinstance needs path param instance_name (a NAME not an id) captured from $.instance_groups[0].instances[0].name on the cluster detail. epasmanualbackup takes NO request body per the docs model (path cluster_id only), mirrors mysql/mariadbmanualbackup. epasexportlog log_type is a fixed enum (alert|audit|slow, data/api_docs.json database/epas/epasexportlog) -- tries all 3 values sequentially (own group each) per the orchestrator brief; registration is PF-blocked (known_issues.json database/epas/epasregisterlogexportconfig, 500 ContactAdminForAssistance) so export is attempted WITHOUT a registered config, same as the mysql/mariadb siblings. epasremovebackuphistories: body key IS ALREADY 'backup_history_number' (verified correct against data/api_docs.json database/epas/epasremovebackuphistories -- no typo present in the existing epas-cluster-subops-a/guarded fragments, contrary to the orchestrator brief's caution); the mysql/postgresql siblings both reconfirmed TODAY that this endpoint (and its unsetbackup sibling) 401 Dbaas.Unauthorized.AuthNFailed even with a correct body + a REAL captured backup_history_number -- a known backend auth quirk (query-string HMAC signing on backup-family endpoints) shared across mysql/mariadb/postgresql/epas/cachestore, NOT a body-shape bug -- reconfirmed once more here for epas specifically (own known_issues.json entry to follow if reproduced). epasunsetbackup similarly 1-shot rechecked here (no known_issues.json entry existed yet for epas specifically before this run). C-group (epascreaterestore, epascreateotherregionreplica, epasswitchovercluster) deliberately EXCLUDED -- each needs its own extra billable cluster, a completed backup, or an ha_enabled=true/replica cluster (mysql precedent: switchover 404 'switchover-host.not-found' on a single-node cluster, structural) -- out of this session's single-cluster/time budget; left as a follow-up lever. register/set/unregister-log-export-config deliberately EXCLUDED from this lifecycle (same convention as the mysql/mariadb siblings) -- register is already a confirmed PF-500 across all 5 DB engines (knowledge/validated-facts.md), and set/unregister are structurally unreachable-2xx downstream of it. Own create-vpc(10.146.0.0/20)/create-subnet(10.146.3.0/24) + adopt:'vpc'/'subnet#db' markers mirroring the mysql/mariadb template -- per the mariadb sibling's LIVE-OBSERVED note, the session-scoped shared_infra fixture actually adopts/provisions a shared VPC and these steps get skipped at runtime; the CIDRs above are kept for schema-consistency with the other version-upgrade lifecycles, not because they're guaranteed to be used. OPERATIONAL LESSON (mariadb sibling, 2026-07-16): invoke via run_in_background:true -- a foreground shell call hitting the harness's own ~2min default timeout gets SIGKILLed WITHOUT running pytest's session teardown, orphaning the shared VPC+subnet. Budget the full session runway for one attempt (create ~2400s + minor-patch settle ~1800s + manual-backup settle ~600s + delete polling), do not split into a second short probe.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "create-vpc",
